														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2829108">
									

<p>I like it!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;but</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;but</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Some of the execution still seems bit wonky to me though&#8212; in particular, you are inconsistent with the verb tenses in the addenda. It's probably best to use past tense for everything in those EXCEPT the MTF log.</p>
<p>Also, and this is more minor, some of the wording in Addendum 2 feels unnatural to me. Like this exchange:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Bravo:</strong> Jesus, that's bright. Command, this skip has managed to heat the air by… a lot. Guess there was a reason it was in a vacuum.</p>
<p><strong>Delta:</strong> My thermometer reads — Wow, it's… uh… melted, actually. We should probably head out pretty soon.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I dunno, this just seems too&#8230; casual? I think the last sentence from each of these agents is unnecessary and kind of obvious.</p>
<p>Also, some of the wording in the last three paragraphs of the article is kind of weird. For example, instead of</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a full investigation by the Ethics Committee took place</p>
</blockquote>
<p>it would probably be better to keep this in the active voice&#8212; &quot;the Ethics Committee conducted a full investigation.&quot; There are a few other sentences in this section that could probably be cleaned up as well, to make it clearer/easier to read.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>All of these are minor things, but definitely noticeable. Still, +1 from me for a quirky little anomaly and an interesting story that I don't think has been done yet.</p>

